v1.0.55 build 76: fix first-time picker frame drop via foreground prewarm & post-frame animation tick

- main.dart: moved _CupertinoPickerPrewarmer to the TOP of the Stack in
  MaterialApp.builder with Opacity(0.005). Previously it was underneath
  MainScaffold, causing Impeller's occlusion culler to completely discard
  its draw calls and skip compiling the OpenGLES shaders. With it on top
  and semi-transparent, Impeller is forced to rasterize glyphs and compile
  shaders during launch, while remaining invisible to the human eye.
- sheet_picker.dart: decoupled CupertinoDatePicker mount from SlideTransition
  ticker start via WidgetsBinding.instance.addPostFrameCallback. In frame 1,
  the widget mounts and rasterizes into RepaintBoundary while the ticker is
  idle (0ms elapsed). In frame 2+, the ticker animates purely translating
  the pre-existing GPU texture, eliminating the 40ms first-frame hitch.
